.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-vpn 1  "rev-stealth-vpn " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-vpn \- VPN IP rotation operations (Surfshark / Gluetun lazy\-rotate\-on\-fail)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth vpn\fR [\fB\-\-output\-format\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
VPN exit\-IP control. `rotate` triggers a provider rotation with the chosen strategy (lazy\-on\-fail / every\-n / interval); `status` probes the current public IP and the VPN container state. All actions are audit\-logged.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-output\-format\fR \fI<OUTPUT_FORMAT>\fR
Output format for this subcommand: `human` (default) or `json`. Shadows the global `\-\-format` for this invocation. Same value enum as the global flag; the JSON output is documented under `docs/json\-schemas/cli/<subcommand>.output.json`
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
rev\-stealth\-vpn\-rotate(1)
Trigger a VPN rotation. With `lazy\-on\-fail`, rotation is skipped unless the failure counter has crossed the threshold
.TP
rev\-stealth\-vpn\-status(1)
Show the current public IP and the VPN container state
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth vpn rotate \-\-strategy lazy\-on\-fail \-\-reason scrape\-failure
  $ rev\-stealth vpn status

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Action completed.
  1  UserError        Bad \-\-provider / \-\-strategy.
  2  TransientError   Provider/container transient failure.
  3  PermanentError   Provider unsupported in this build.
  7  Leak             Post\-action leak detected (fail\-closed).

ENV:
  REV_SCRAPING_REQUIRE_VPN  When `1`, enforces VPN\-required guard policy\-wide.
  VPN_INSTANCES             Pool of named VPN instances (config.vpn_instances).
